Camille, Gretchen,<br />
<br />
Recommendation: withdraw Count II and the allegation that a 2012 undertakin=
g exists, before Thackston moves on it.<br />
<br />
The basis is not that we cannot prove Count II. The basis is that Count II =
is not true, and I want the file to say that in those words.<br />
<br />
The journal archive was searched twice, the second time with a wider mailbo=
x list, a longer date range and additional terms, full text including attac=
hments. It produced no deficiency letter, no undertaking and no corrective =
action commitment, and it produced our own examiner telling the registrant =
in 2013 that the examination closed clean. The EXAMTRAC restore produced th=
e complete work paper set and a closing recommendation of no deficiencies. =
The disposition code we hold is C-1 rather than C-2, which is not what the =
C-4 mapping produces. The registrant's compliance officer, who has been in =
the seat continuously since 2011, states that no undertaking was requested =
or given.<br />
<br />
On where the allegation came from, I have traced it. The 2013 branch tracki=
ng spreadsheet row reading "OTA - undertaking obtained, follow up next cycl=
e" sits directly below a row for a different Philadelphia registrant examin=
ed under an adjacent number, and that registrant did give an undertaking th=
at year in a matter that has nothing to do with this one. The initials in t=
he cell match the other registrant, not Ottoway Trask. Somebody typed a row=
 one line off in a spreadsheet in 2013 and we pleaded it in 2024.<br />
<br />
Counts I and III are unaffected and I would not disturb them. The books and=
 records deficiencies are documented from 2021 forward and are not in dispu=
te in any serious way.<br />
